# vigia-web: Use Cases na UI

## Camadas

```
pages/shared (UI) → core/usecases (*Service.execute) → core/services (HTTP/auth/storage)
```

- **UI** (`pages/`, `shared/components/`): só injeta **use cases** (`@core/usecases`) para ações de negócio e carregamento de dados.
- **Use cases** (`core/usecases/<nome>/<nome>.service.ts`): orquestram mappers + services; expõem `execute(...)`.
- **Services** (`core/services/`): HTTP, sessão, storage — infraestrutura.

## Permitido chamar AuthService / HTTP services direto

- Interceptors, guards, e o próprio corpo da use case.
- Services de UI transversal sem API de domínio (ex.: `ThemeService`, `LanguageService`, `MessageService`).

## Proibido

```typescript
// ❌ página/componente de feature
private readonly devicesService = inject(DevicesService);
private readonly authService = inject(AuthService);
await this.authService.login(email, password);
this.devicesService.getDevices().subscribe(...);

// ✅
private readonly login = inject(LoginService);
private readonly getDevices = inject(GetDevicesService);
await this.login.execute(email, password);
firstValueFrom(this.getDevices.execute());
```

## Ao adicionar feature

1. Criar/estender use case em `core/usecases/<feature>/` com `execute`.
2. Exportar em `core/usecases/index.ts`.
3. Página/componente injeta só a use case.
4. Testes da UI mockam a use case; testes da use case mockam os services.
